**VULNERABILITY NAME or TYPE: Redundant Conditional Check in hasPlayerWagered**
'''
DETAILED DESCRIPTION:
The function `hasPlayerWagered(address player)` uses an if-else statement to return a boolean value based on the condition `wagers[player] > 0`. Since `wagers[player] > 0` already evaluates to a boolean (`true` or `false`), the explicit if-else construct is redundant, adding unnecessary code complexity and additional gas costs. The current implementation:
```
if(wagers[player] > 0)
{
    return true;
}
else
{
    return false;
}
```
can be simplified to a single return statement.

Recommended mitigation:
Replace the entire if-else block with `return wagers[player] > 0;` to reduce gas consumption and improve code readability without altering functionality.
'''
