Unnecessary Comparison Identified.
```
VULNERABILITY NAME or TYPE: Unnecessary Comparison (Redundant Boolean Conditional)
'''
DETAILED DESCRIPTION: The function `hasPlayerWagered(address player)` contains a redundant conditional that compares a boolean expression to return true or false explicitly. The code uses:
```solidity
if(wagers[player] > 0) {
    return true;
} else {
    return false;
}
```
This can be simplified to a single return statement: `return wagers[player] > 0;`. The explicit `if-else` with boolean returns is unnecessary because the condition `wagers[player] > 0` already evaluates to a boolean value. This unnecessary comparison reduces readability and introduces code clutter without any functional benefit.

Recommended mitigation: Replace the entire if-else block with a direct return of the condition:
```solidity
function hasPlayerWagered(address player) public view returns (bool) {
    return wagers[player] > 0;
}
```
